// The windows' part of a pixel of footprint fp (A, B weighted; the returned weight's rest is the cube's, read at its
// level 0): the two levels its footprint falls between, as the cube's trilinear read would have picked them had it
// those levels; finer than the finest level, that level magnified. Only levels lo..hi take part (the tile's static
// window sits between two calls: the levels finer than it, then it, then the coarser ones).
float geoWinRead(vec3 n, float fp, int lo, int hi, out vec4 A, out vec4 B){
  A=vec4(0.); B=vec4(0.);
  float L=geoWinInfo.x;
  if(L<=0.||hi<lo) return 0.;
  float lam=-log2(fp/(geoAlbedoInfo.x*geoAlbedoTexel(n)));
  if(lam<=0.) return 0.;
