  // and what c's window or fade-in lacks), and what the two lack the coarser levels fill in turn (their windows
  // reach farther), before the far bakes' windows at 24 m and up. Continuous in the footprint: were level c+1
  // given only f, a pixel outside c's window would drop from the next level to the one after as f reaches 0
  // (a seam along a constant-footprint curve).
  float f1=float(c)<last?1.-w0:0.;
#else
  float f1=f;
#endif
